    qa: [
      { q: 'What happens to the air sealed inside the engine?', choices: ['It is replaced by fresh air each time', 'It is turned into steam by the fire', 'It leaks slowly out past the piston', 'It expands and contracts repeatedly'], answer: 3, why: '第3段落：同じ空気が何度もふくらんだりちぢんだりする。毎回新しい空気に入れかわる、蒸気に変わる、ピストンからもれるとは書かれていない。' },
      { q: 'Why did the engine fail to replace steam on a large scale?', choices: ['It needed far more fuel than steam engines', 'It could not change speed easily', 'It was too loud for use in factories', 'It required a large boiler of water'], answer: 1, why: '第5段落：急に力が必要になっても速さを簡単に変えられなかった。燃料が多くいる、うるさい、大きなボイラーが必要とは書かれていない。' },
    ],
